>> title: Queso Fresco
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: cheese, milk, mexican, fresh, condiment
>> counters: Panadería, Taquería, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: queso blanco, fresh cheese, mexican fresh cheese, ranchero cheese, queso ranchero
>> pairs-with: salsa-roja, mexican-red-rice
>> servings: 8
>> time: 5 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the milk has to reach 185°F and not be ultra-pasteurised, or it never curds at all and the pot cannot be tried again
>> step.1: heat to 185°F (85°C)
>> step.2: stir in the acid, stand 20 min
>> step.3: drain 45 min
>> step.4: salt and press 2 hr
>> step.5: chill 2 hr

Heat @whole milk{1%gal}(3.8 L) and @heavy cream{1%cup}(240 mL) in a #heavy pot{} to 185°F (85°C), stirring from the bottom so the milk does not catch.

Stir @distilled white vinegar{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and @lime juice{2%Tbs}(30 mL) into @&(~1)hot milk{}, take the pot off the heat and ~stand{20%min} until the curds pull together and the whey under them runs clear.

Ladle @&(~1)curds{} into a #colander{} lined with damp cheesecloth and ~drain{45%min}.

Work @fine sea salt{2%tsp} through @&(~1)drained curds{}, gather the cloth into a flat disc and ~press{2%hr} under a plate and a full can.

Chill @&(~1)pressed cheese{} ~chill{2%hr} before crumbling.
